<title>UK: BGB unit ups 10-year fix/rev FRN to 200 bln lire.</title>
<headline>BGB unit ups 10-year fix/rev FRN to 200 bln lire.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to 200 billion lire from 150 billion lire, joint lead managers Credito Italiano and Morgan Stanley said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BGB FINANCE IRELAND BV</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  BGB GROUP</p>
<p> AMT   *200 BLN ITL   COUPON   **9.0	 MATURITY    13.FEB.07</p>
<p> TYPE   FIX/REV FRN   ISS PRICE *101.425   PAY DATE    13.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.0	 REOFFER    99.75     SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AA1/AAA   DENOMS (M) 10	  LISTING     LUX</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    0.375     HOME CTRY  1.625     GOV LAW     ENGLISH</p>
<p> NOTES     *ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED FOR 150 BLN ITL AT AN ISSUE</p>
<p>		PRICE OF 100.175.</p>
<p>	    **FOR YEARS 1-4, THEN 19.5 PCT LESS (2 X 6M LIBOR)</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF MTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
